user/blobs/ contains prebuilt TEST binaries and shared libraries that are third-party software redistributed unmodified or linked into test programs. Their sources are not part of this repository; obtain them from the upstream projects:
  - Ubuntu GNU C Library 2.39 (libc.so.6, libm.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, libnss_*.so.2): LGPL-2.1-or-later. Many linux_*.elf test programs are statically linked against glibc; their own sources are in user/poc/ so they can be relinked.
  - GCC runtime libraries (libstdc++.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1): GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception.
  - OpenSSL 3.x (statically linked into linux_tls.elf): Apache-2.0.
  - MinGW-w64 runtime and import libraries (linked into win_*.exe / *.dll): mostly public domain / ZPL-2.1 / MIT-style; see the mingw-w64 project.
user/seh/deloxy_seh.c is part of Deloxy (its `unwind code` interpretation follows the public x64 unwind-info format documented by Microsoft and the algorithms used by the Wine and ReactOS projects, re-implemented from the specification, not copied).
user/poc/tls/ holds throw-away test certificates and keys, used only by the local TLS test. They protect nothing.
The optional full ISO (tools/mkfull-iso.sh) additionally embeds CPython 3.12 (PSF License) and the `file` utility (BSD-2-Clause) taken from the build machine; they are not stored in this repository.
